    So <math|3R/<around|(|\<lambda\> x<rsup|3>|)>\<to\>1>: the remainder
    <strong|cancels the cube> (the dip: <math|R> changes sign, Wick term below, cube above). Field equation:
    <math|q*x=<around|(|q-q<rsub|0>|)>m<rsub|q>+\<omega\><rsub|q>>, only linear
    confinement.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The price of clipping>

    \;

    <math|f<rsup|c>=f<rsub|1>+\<cal-C\>*f<rsub|2>>, with
    <math|f<rsub|1>=-<frac|\<lambda\>|3><around|(|x<rsup|3>+3S*x|)>>,
    <math|f<rsub|2>> the first tree, <math|\<kappa\><rsub|q>> a smooth clip at <math|<around|\||x|\|>\<sim\>r<rsub|q>>, <math|\<cal-C\>*f<rsub|2>=\<kappa\><rsub|q>'\<cdot\>
    f<rsub|2>\<circ\>\<kappa\><rsub|q>>. For
    <math|<around|\||x|\|>\<geqslant\>2r<rsub|q>>, the Burgers defect is
    exactly

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-S\><rsub|q>=S<rsup|2>f<rsub|1>f<rsub|1>'\<approx\><frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|3>S<rsup|2>x<rsup|5>,
    </equation*>

    of order <math|<around|(|q/\<lambda\>|)><rsup|1/2>> at the edge of the
    clip: not integrable in <math|q>.

    <\equation*>
      <space|0.17em>\<mathd\> R<rsub|q>=-<around|[|\<cal-S\><rsub|q>+S<rsup|2><around|(|f<rsup|c>|)>'R<rsub|q>|]><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>
      q+\<Xi\><rsup|R><rsub|q><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>
      W<rsub|q>,<space|1em><text|bracket>\<approx\><frac|\<lambda\><rsup|2>|3>S<rsup|2>x<rsup|5>-\<lambda\>
      S<rsup|2>x<rsup|2>R.
    </equation*>

    The source and the dissipation cancel for the true
    <math|R\<sim\><frac|\<lambda\>|3> x<rsup|3>>: separate estimates give
    nothing.

    Tails independent of <math|R>: on one site from the posterior moment, but
    not uniform on the lattice (negative bare mass).

    More orders do not help: the tree series has radius
    <math|<frac|2|3>r<rsub|q>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Integrating the cube>

    \;

    Solve the transport part of the flow exactly:

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>f+S<rsup|2>f*f<rprime|'>=0,<space|1em>
      f<rsub|\<infty\>>=-<frac|\<lambda\>|3>
      x<rsup|3><space|1em>\<Rightarrow\><space|1em>
      f<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>=-<frac|\<lambda\>|3> y<rsup|3>,<space|1em>
      q*y+<frac|\<lambda\>|3> y<rsup|3>=q*x.
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      sup<rsub|x><around|\||F<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>-f<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>|\|>\<leqslant\>2C<rsub|\<ast\>><around|(|<frac|\<lambda\>|3q>|)><rsup|1/2>,<space|1em>
      C<rsub|\<ast\>>\<less\><frac|1|2>.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|y<rsub|q><around|(|\<Phi\><rsub|q>|)>=Y<rsub|q>>:
      <strong|this is the forecast coordinate>.
      <math|F<rsub|q>-f<rsub|q>=K<rsub|q>Z<rsub|q>>, and <math|Z> is the
      posterior mean minus the mode.

      <item>The defect is <math|q*b<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>>: bounded for all
      fields. The trees are in <math|x\<mapsto\> y>; the cube does not flow
      in <math|y>, so only loops are clipped.

      <item>The cube is coercive in <math|y>: <math|q*y+<frac|\<lambda\>|3>
      y<rsup|3>=q*\<Phi\><rsub|q>>.
    </itemize>

    <small|Not a no-go theorem: it rules out only estimating <math|R> as a
    small perturbation of the frozen cube. Integrating the cube in the
    original field is possible, but on the lattice its loop defect must still
    be renormalised; that route is not proved here.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <cqft-part-title|Renormalisation: why two of them>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture<nbsp>6>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Approximating the exact force>

We seek an explicit force with a small <strong|defect>, not the full
    solution of the nonlinear flow.

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>\<cal-F\><rsub|q>=-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|H<rsup|<math-up|ex>><rsub|q>|)><rsup|2>>D<rsup|2>\<cal-F\><rsub|q>,<space|2em>H<rsup|<math-up|ex>><rsub|q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+D\<cal-F\><rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>.
    </equation*>

    At infinite resolution: <math|\<cal-F\><rsub|\<infty\>>=U'+\<mu\><rsub|N>y>,
    with <math|U'<around|(|y|)>=<frac|\<lambda\>|3>y<rsup|3>>.

    <\enumerate>
      <item>Insert the bare cube into the response and the vertex: a
      <strong|one-loop seed>.

      <item>Feed each approximation back into the equation: <strong|two
      correction steps>.

      <item>Estimate the remaining defect in the backward equation for
      <math|Z>.
    </enumerate>

    <\myframed>
      First separate the linear flow: it produces the divergent mass
      counterterm and cannot be treated as a small nonlinear error.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Why the linear term must be separated>

Insert <math|U'> into the loop, with
    <math|G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+\<lambda\>y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>>:

    <\equation*>
      -<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|G<rsub|q><rsup|2>>D<rsup|2>U'<around|(|y|)><around|(|x|)>=-\<lambda\>y<around|(|x|)>G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><rsup|2><around|(|x,x|)>.
    </equation*>

    Its linear Taylor coefficient is

    <\equation*>
      -\<lambda\>a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>y<around|(|x|)>,<space|2em>a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>=C<rsub|q><rsup|2><around|(|x,x|)>.
    </equation*>

    In three dimensions <math|a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>> has continuum size
    <math|q<rsup|-1/2>>: its integral to infinity diverges. At fixed lattice
    cutoff it is finite, but grows with <math|N>.

    <\myframed>
      This is the <strong|tadpole>. Further insertions also produce the
      logarithmic <strong|sunset>. Keep the linear flow in a running mass;
      iterate only the nonlinear remainder.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The projections <math|\<Pi\>> and <math|\<Pi\><rprime|'>>>

    For a smooth odd force <math|f>, and a translation-invariant operator
    <math|L=<around|\<langle\>|L|\<rangle\>>I+L<rsup|\<circ\>>> (constant mode plus centred part):

    <\equation*>
      <around|(|\<Pi\>f|)><around|(|y|)>=f<around|(|y|)>-Df<around|(|0|)>y,<space|2em><around|(|\<Pi\><rprime|'>f|)><around|(|y|)>=f<around|(|y|)>-<around|\<langle\>|Df<around|(|0|)>|\<rangle\>>y.
    </equation*>

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|\<Pi\>f> starts at <strong|cubic order>;
      <math|\<Pi\><rprime|'>f=\<Pi\>f+<around|(|Df<around|(|0|)>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>y>
      removes only the <strong|scalar> part of the linear jet.

      <item>The divergences (tadpole, sunset) are <strong|constant modes>.
      The centred part of the linear flow is integrable at infinity.
    </itemize>

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsub|q>=U'+M<rsub|q>y+\<ell\><rsub|q>,<space|2em>\<Pi\>\<ell\><rsub|q>=\<ell\><rsub|q>,<space|1em>M<rsub|q>=\<mu\><rsub|q>I+\<Theta\><rsub|q>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      <math|\<ell\>> and the centred kernel <math|\<Theta\>>: integrate from
      <math|\<infty\>>, by the same finite iteration. Scalar mass <math|\<mu\>>: solve exactly, fixed at an auxiliary large scale <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>> (with <math|g<rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>> small).
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Scales and power counting>

    \;

    <\equation*>
      g<rsub|q>=\<lambda\>*q<rsup|-1/2><around|(|<text|dimensionless
      coupling>|)>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      r<rsub|q>=<around|(|q/\<lambda\>|)><rsup|1/2><around|(|\<lambda\>*r<rsub|q><rsup|2>=q:<text|nonlinearity>\<approx\><text|regulator>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Free field at resolution <math|q>: free field <math|X<rsub|q>>, <math|<math-up|Var>X<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|1/2>>,
    typical size <math|q<rsup|1/4>=g<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|q>\<ll\>r<rsub|q>>.

    Rooted norm of a vertex <math|T<around|(|x<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,x<rsub|k>|)>>
    and field ball:

    <\equation*>
      s<around|(|T|)>=max<rsub|i> sup<rsub|x<rsub|i>>
      <big|int><around|\||T|\|>*<big|prod><rsub|j\<ne\>i>\<mathd\>x<rsub|j>,<space|2em><math-ss|S><rsub|k><around|(|f|)>=sup<rsub|\<cal-B\><rsub|q>> s*<around|(|D<rsup|k-1>*f|)>,<space|2em>\<cal-B\><rsub|q>=<around|<left|{|2>|<around|\<\|\|\>|y|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<less\>2*r<rsub|q>|<right|}|2>>.
    </equation*>

    Natural size of the <math|k>-leg vertex of the <strong|loop corrections>:

    <\equation*>
      <math-ss|S><rsub|k>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q>*<space|0.17em>q*<space|0.17em>r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>*<space|2em><around|(|k=4:\<lambda\>*g<rsub|q>|)>.
    </equation*>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The loop estimate>

    Root one leg of a closed loop and follow the loop: two of its
    propagators are estimated in <math|L<rsup|2>> (this gives the bubble
    <math|a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>>), all the others in operator norm (each
    <math|q<rsup|-1>>).

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Loop estimate>

      A closed loop with <math|p> vertices:
      <math|s<around|(|<text|loop>|)>\<leqslant\>C*a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>*<space|0.17em>q<rsup|-<around|(|p-1|)>>*<big|prod><rsub|i>s<around|(|T<rsub|i>|)>>
      (two propagators in <math|L<rsup|2>>, the others in operator norm).
      After the <math|q> integration a one-loop term is of size
      <math|g<rsub|q>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>; every further loop gains a
      factor <math|g<rsub|q>>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Computing the one-loop seed>

Project the bare loop before integrating:

    <\equation*>
      \<Pi\><around*|[|-\<lambda\>y<around|(|x|)>G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><rsup|2><around|(|x,x|)>|]>=-\<lambda\>y<around|(|x|)><around|[|G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><rsup|2><around|(|x,x|)>-a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>|]>.
    </equation*>

    Use <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>G<rsub|q>=-G<rsub|q><rsup|2>> and
    <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>C<rsub|q>=-C<rsub|q><rsup|2>>. With zero
    boundary value at infinity:

    <\myframed>
      <\equation*>
        \<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>><rsub|q><around|(|y|)><around|(|x|)>=\<lambda\>y<around|(|x|)><around|[|G<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><around|(|x,x|)>-C<rsub|q><around|(|x,x|)>|]>.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>

    The leading term is the bubble:

    <\equation*>
      -\<lambda\><rsup|2>y<around|(|x|)><big|int>C<rsub|q><around|(|x,z|)><rsup|2>y<around|(|z|)><rsup|2>\<mathd\>z.
    </equation*>

    Four-leg size: <math|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>=\<lambda\>g<rsub|q>>.
    This is the seed <math|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>>: the superscript counts loops.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The seed in graphs>

    <with|par-mode|center|<\script-output|tikz|default>
      \\documentclass[tikz]{standalone}

      \\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

      \\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}

      \\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}

      \\usetikzlibrary{calc,decorations.markings}

