      \;
    </script-output|<image|<tuple|<#>|ps>|300pt|||>>>

    The seed as one-loop graphs: lines <math|C<rsub|q>>, a vertex
    <math|\<lambda\> y<rsup|2>> with its two external fields at each corner.
    The <math|j>-th ring has <math|2j> legs and coefficient
    <math|<around|(|-1|)><rsup|j+1>/<around|(|2j|)>>; <math|D> marks one leg,
    giving the force. The series sums to a logarithm, with radius of
    convergence <math|r<rsub|q>>. The quartic ring is the bubble.

  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Splitting the flow and deriving the iteration>

    For <math|\<cal-F\>=U'+M*y+\<ell\>>, the loop map

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]>=-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsup|2>>D<rsup|2><around|(|U'+\<ell\>|)>,<space|1em>R=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>+D<around|(|U'+\<ell\>|)>|)><rsup|-1>.
    </equation*>

    Three equations of different nature:

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>\<ell\>=\<Pi\>\<cal-T\><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]>,<space|1em>\<partial\><rsub|q>\<Theta\>=<around|(|D\<cal-T\><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]><around|(|0|)>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>,<space|1em>\<partial\><rsub|q>\<mu\>=<around|\<langle\>|D\<cal-T\><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]><around|(|0|)>|\<rangle\>>.
    </equation*>

    <strong|Fix a trial scalar path <math|\<mu\>>> (determined at the end as a fixed point, "Closing the mass path"). Level masses
    <math|M<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>=\<mu\>I+\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>>, sources
    <math|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>=D\<cal-T\><around|[|M<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>|]><around|(|0|)>> (not the Brownian motion <math|B>), zero-field response <math|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|0,q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>>:

    <\myframed>
      <\equation*>
        \<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>><rsub|q>=-<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\>\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|[|M<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>|]>\<mathd\>s,<space|1em>\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>><rsub|q>=-<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>><around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>\<mathd\>s,<space|1em>j=1,2.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>

    With <math|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|0|]>>=0>, <math|M<rsup|<around|[|0|]>>=0>, the case <math|j=0> is the seed step without mass, <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>=\<Pi\>\<cal-T\><around|[|0,0|]>>,
    and <math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>=0> (the tadpole is local). Output:
    <math|<around|(|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>,\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>|)><around|[|\<mu\>|]>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Centre before taking absolute values>

    A centred kernel <math|\<Theta\><around|(|z|)>=\<Theta\><around|(|0,z|)>> is
    measured by its first moment
    <math|v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\>|)>=<big|int>d<around|(|0,z|)><around|\||\<Theta\><around|(|z|)>|\|>\<mathd\>z>,
    <math|d> the torus distance. For an even kernel,
    <math|\<Theta\><with|math-font|Bbb|1>=0> means that the diagonal cancels
    the off-diagonal mass. With <math|<around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|z>f|)><around|(|x|)>=f<around|(|x+z|)>>,
    <math|\<delta\><rsub|z><rsup|2>=\<sigma\><rsub|z>+\<sigma\><rsub|-z>-2I>,

    <\equation*>
      C<rsub|q>\<Theta\>=<frac|1|2><big|int>\<Theta\><around|(|z|)>\<delta\><rsub|z><rsup|2>C<rsub|q>\<mathd\>z.
    </equation*>

    <strong|The absolute row norm discards the cancellation.>
    For a lattice step <math|h> in direction <math|e>, take

    <\equation*>
      \<Theta\><rsub|h>=<frac|a|2h><around|(|\<sigma\><rsub|he>+\<sigma\><rsub|-he>-2I|)>,<space|2em>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|h>|)>=a,<space|1em><around|\<\|\|\>|\<Theta\><rsub|h>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>=<frac|2a|h>.
    </equation*>

    The row norm diverges as <math|h\<to\>0>; the first moment stays bounded.

    <\myframed>
      Estimate the signed product <math|C<rsub|q>\<Theta\>> first.
      The quantity needed by the loop is the kernel after resolvent
      smoothing, not the absolute mass of <math|\<Theta\>> itself.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Smoothing turns cancellation into a moment bound>

    The resolvent smooths on length scale <math|q<rsup|-1/2>>:

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|\<delta\><rsub|z><rsup|2>C<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<leqslant\>C*q<rsup|-1/2>d<around|(|0,z|)>.
    </equation*>

    Scale check: integrate the heat-kernel translation bound
    <math|C*d<around|(|0,z|)>t<rsup|-1/2>> against
    <math|\<mathe\><rsup|-qt>\<mathd\>t>.

    <\myframed>
      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|C<rsub|q>\<Theta\>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<leqslant\>C*q<rsup|-1/2><big|int>d<around|(|0,z|)><around|\||\<Theta\><around|(|z|)>|\|>\<mathd\>z=C*q<rsup|-1/2>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\>|)>.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>

    The iteration (next slides) supplies exactly the compensating moment:

    <\equation*>
      v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2><space|1em>\<Longrightarrow\><space|1em> q<rsup|-1/2>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1>=g<rsub|q><rsup|2>.
    </equation*>

    <small|A bound by <math|d<around|(|0,z|)><rsup|2>> loses a logarithm; one
    distance power, with <math|q<rsup|-1/2>>, suffices (Lemma<nbsp>19.3 of the
    Supplement).>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The small factor in a resolvent comparison>

    The field-dependent response also receives this cancellation. With
    <math|V=\<lambda\>y<rsup|2>> and <math|G=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+V|)><rsup|-1>>,

    <\equation*>
      G\<Theta\>=<around|(|I-GV|)>C<rsub|q>\<Theta\>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|I-GV|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>\<to\>\<infty\>>\<leqslant\>2.
    </equation*>

    The bounded Neumann series for the full <math|R> then gives

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<\|\|\>|R\<delta\>M|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>\<to\>\<infty\>>\<leqslant\>C\<rho\><rsub|q>,<space|1em>\<rho\><rsub|q>=<frac|<around|\||\<delta\>\<mu\><rsub|q>|\|>|q>+q<rsup|-1/2>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<delta\>\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>.
    </equation*>

    Holding the nonlinear correction fixed,
    <math|\<delta\>R=-R\<delta\>M<wide|R|^>> (<math|<wide|R|^>> the response at
    mass <math|M-\<delta\>M>) has row norm
    <math|\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsub|q>/q> and row <math|L<rsup|2>> norm <math|sup<rsub|x><around|\<\|\|\>|\<delta\>R<around|(|x,\<cdot\>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|L<rsup|2>>>
    <math|\<lesssim\>\<rho\><rsub|q><sqrt|a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>>>.

    <\myframed>
      A marked propagator gains the relative factor <math|\<rho\><rsub|q>>:
      for <math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>> in the second correction,
      <math|\<rho\><rsub|q>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q><rsup|2>>; for two scalar paths,
      see "Mass differences" below.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Centring the source removes local terms>

    Separate the source at level <math|j> into tadpole and correction vertex:

    <\equation*>
      B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>=-\<lambda\><math-up|Tr><around|(|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2>|)>I+E<rsub|q>,<space|1em>E<rsub|q>=-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2>>T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>,<space|1em>T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>=D<rsup|3>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>.
    </equation*>

    Write <math|E<rsub|q><with|math-font|Bbb|1>=e<rsub|q><with|math-font|Bbb|1>>.
    The constant mode contains the whole local contribution:

    <\equation*>
      <around|\<langle\>|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|\<rangle\>>=-\<lambda\><math-up|Tr><around|(|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2>|)>+e<rsub|q>,<space|2em><around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>=E<rsub|q>-e<rsub|q>I.
    </equation*>

    The tadpole cancels; so does any term <math|c<rsub|q>I>.
    Off-diagonal entries stay unchanged. Since <math|d<around|(|0,0|)>=0>,

    <\equation*>
      v<rsub|1><around|(|<around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>|)>=v<rsub|1><around|(|E<rsub|q>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      Centring removes the local obstruction. The remaining spatial
      estimate must come from the first moment of the nonlinear vertex.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The iteration produces the first-moment bound>

    <\with|font-size|0.9>

      Four-leg vertex <math|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>> of <math|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>>, proved below level by level (<math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>> needs only the bubble <math|T<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>>, <math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>> only <math|T<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>>, at <math|M<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>=\<mu\>I>):

      <\equation*>
        s<around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>+<sqrt|q>v<rsub|1><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>,<space|1em><text|hence><space|1em>v<rsub|1><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1>.
      </equation*>

      Keep the distance between the uncontracted legs of <math|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>>; since <math|sup<rsub|u,v><around|\||<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2><around|(|u,v|)>|\|>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-1/2>>,

      <\equation*>
        v<rsub|1><around|(|<around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>|)>=v<rsub|1><around|(|E<rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-1/2>v<rsub|1><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-3/2>.
      </equation*>

      Integrate with zero boundary value at infinity:

      <\equation*>
        v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>v<rsub|1><around|(|<around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|s>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>|)>\<mathd\>s\<leqslant\>C\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>.
      </equation*>

      <\myframed>
        Uniformly in <math|N>: <math|\<eta\><rsub|q><around|(|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q><rsup|2>>,
        and one more <math|g> for the difference,
        <math|\<eta\><rsub|q><around|(|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>-\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>,
        with <math|\<eta\><rsub|q><around|(|\<Theta\>|)>=q<rsup|-1/2>v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\>|)>>.
      </myframed>
    </with>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|First correction: insert the seed>

Set <math|R<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>=<around|(|K+M<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>+DU'+D\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>>|)><rsup|-1>>
    and <math|\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>=\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>-\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>>.
    Subtract the bare loop from the loop containing the seed:

    <\equation*>
      \<delta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q>=<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\><around*|[|<math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)><rsup|2>-G<rsup|2>>D<rsup|2>U'+<math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)><rsup|2>>D<rsup|2>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|]><rsub|s>\<mathd\>s.
    </equation*>

    <strong|Two changes:> the propagators and the vertex.

    <\equation*>
      R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>-G=-R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>><around|(|\<mu\>+D\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)>G,<space|2em>M<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>=\<mu\>I.
    </equation*>

    The insertion <math|<around|(|\<mu\>+D\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)>/q> is
    <math|O<around|(|g<rsub|q>|)>>. One extra loop gives

    <\equation*>
      <math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>g<rsub|s>s<rsup|1/2>r<rsub|s><rsup|-4>\<mathd\>s=\<lambda\><rsup|3>q<rsup|-1>=\<lambda\>g<rsub|q><rsup|2>.
    </equation*>

    All factors inside the integral are evaluated at scale <math|s>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Second correction: insert the first correction>

Put <math|\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>=\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>-\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>>.
    Subtract the first two Picard equations:

    <\equation*>
      \<delta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>=<frac|1|2><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\><around*|[|<math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)><rsup|2>-<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)><rsup|2>>D<rsup|2><around|(|U'+\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|1|]>>|)>+<math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)><rsup|2>>D<rsup|2>\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]><rsub|s>\<mathd\>s.
    </equation*>

    The marked insertion is now the first correction itself, nonlinear and centred:

    <\equation*>
      R<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>-R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>=-R<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><around|(|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>+D\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)>R<rsup|<around|[|1|]>>,
    </equation*>

    where <math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>> costs <math|\<eta\><rsub|q><around|(|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q><rsup|2>> (above).

    <\equation*>
      <math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>g<rsub|s><rsup|2>s<rsup|1/2>r<rsub|s><rsup|-4>\<mathd\>s=<frac|2|3>\<lambda\><rsup|4>q<rsup|-3/2>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      Four-leg sizes: seed <math|\<lambda\>g<rsub|q>>, first correction
      <math|\<lambda\>g<rsub|q><rsup|2>>, second correction
      <math|\<lambda\>g<rsub|q><rsup|3>>.
    </myframed>

    <small|For squared propagators use
    <math|A<rsup|2>-B<rsup|2>=A<around|(|A-B|)>+<around|(|A-B|)>B>;
    no commutativity is assumed.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Following a spatial distance through a loop>

    At zero field, set
    <math|W<rsub|q><around|(|T|)>=s<around|(|T|)>+<sqrt|q>v<rsub|1><around|(|T|)>>.
    Mark two external legs and follow their distance around the loop.

    <\itemize>
      <item>A displacement inside a vertex is controlled by that vertex's
      first moment.

      <item>A displacement along a propagator is controlled by its
      weighted <math|L<rsup|1>> or <math|L<rsup|2>> bound. The triangle
      inequality distributes the external distance over these pieces.
    </itemize>

    For <math|p> vertices and <math|p> propagators:

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|q><around|(|<text|loop>|)>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|-1/2>q<rsup|-<around|(|p-1|)>><big|prod><rsub|i=1><rsup|p>W<rsub|q><around|(|T<rsub|i>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      The weight <math|<sqrt|q>> makes a distance of order
      <math|q<rsup|-1/2>> dimensionless: the weighted loop has the same
      scale powers as the unweighted loop.
    </myframed>

    <small|Keep within-vertex moments: smoothing the propagators cannot
    supply spatial localisation for an arbitrary nonlocal vertex.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Integrating preserves the moment weight>

    A loop difference with relative size <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|s>> has a marked vertex or propagator. With <math|\<delta\>\<cal-T\><rsub|s>=\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|[|M,\<ell\>|]>-\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|[|M,<wide|\<ell\>|^>|]>>, the weighted comparison gives

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|s><around|(|\<mathD\><rsup|k-1>\<delta\>\<cal-T\><rsub|s><around|(|0|)>|)>\<lesssim\>\<varepsilon\><rsub|s>s<rsup|1/2>r<rsub|s><rsup|-k>.
    </equation*>

    For <math|s\<geqslant\>q>, <math|<sqrt|q>\<leqslant\><sqrt|s>>:

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|q><around*|(|<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>A<rsub|s>\<mathd\>s|)>\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>><around|(|s<around|(|A<rsub|s>|)>+<sqrt|q>v<rsub|1><around|(|A<rsub|s>|)>|)>\<mathd\>s\<leqslant\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>W<rsub|s><around|(|A<rsub|s>|)>\<mathd\>s.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      First correction: <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|s>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|s>>.
      Second correction: <math|\<varepsilon\><rsub|s>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|s><rsup|2>>.
    </myframed>

    <math|\<Pi\>> subtracts only a linear force, so it leaves all
    <math|k\<geqslant\>4> vertices unchanged. The field supremum also
    propagates, since <math|\<cal-B\><rsub|q>\<subseteq\>\<cal-B\><rsub|s>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The four-leg moment after two corrections>

    Write <math|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>=\<mathD\><rsup|3>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>>.
    The seed is the bubble:

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|q><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|1|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2><big|int><around|(|1+<sqrt|q>d<around|(|0,z|)>|)>C<rsub|q><around|(|z|)><rsup|2>\<mathd\>z\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>.
    </equation*>

    For the increments, integrate the weighted loop bounds:

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|q><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q>-T<rsup|<around|[|1|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|3><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-2>\<mathd\>s=\<lambda\><rsup|3>q<rsup|-1>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      W<rsub|q><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>-T<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|4><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-5/2>\<mathd\>s=<frac|2|3>\<lambda\><rsup|4>q<rsup|-3/2>.
    </equation*>

    <\myframed>
      For <math|j=1,2,3>,
      <math|s<around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>+<sqrt|q>v<rsub|1><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2><around|(|1+g<rsub|q>+g<rsub|q><rsup|2>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1/2>>.
    </myframed>

    <small|The <math|10\<to\>8\<to\>6> leg budget supplies the higher
    vertices needed by both comparisons. Thus
    <math|v<rsub|1><around|(|T<rsup|<around|[|j|]>><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|2>q<rsup|-1>>.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The mass>

    Impose the <strong|scalar> part of the linear flow for the final
    approximation <math|M=M<rsup|<around|[|3|]>>=\<mu\>I+\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>>, with <math|R<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|0,q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>>:

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>\<mu\><rsub|q>=\<beta\><rsub|q>=<around|\<langle\>|B<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>|\<rangle\>>,<space|1em>B<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>=-\<lambda\><math-up|Tr><around|(|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2>|)>I-<frac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|<around|(|R<rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|0,q>|)><rsup|2>>D<rsup|3>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>,
    </equation*>

    with <math|\<mu\><rsub|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>=b<rsub|\<ast\>>>,
    <math|<around|\||b<rsub|\<ast\>>|\|>\<leqslant\> B<rsub|0>\<lambda\>
    q<rsub|\<ast\>><rsup|1/2>>, at an <strong|auxiliary scale>
    <math|q<rsub|\<ast\>>>. The centred part of <math|B<rsup|<around|[|3|]>>> is
    not imposed. Bare mass <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>=<math-up|lim><rsub|q\<to\>\<infty\>>\<mu\><rsub|q>>:
    an output of the flow. <math|\<beta\>> depends on the whole path <math|\<mu\>> through <math|\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>><around|[|\<mu\>|]>>: a fixed point ("Closing the mass path").
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The defect after the second correction>

    The bounded-field approximation:

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-F\><rsup|o><rsub|q>=U'+M<rsub|q>y+\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>><rsub|q>,<space|2em>\<partial\><rsub|q>\<mu\>=<around|\<langle\>|D\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>|]><around|(|0|)>|\<rangle\>>.
    </equation*>

    The approximations use the preceding level,
    <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>=\<Pi\>\<cal-T\><around|[|M<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]>>,
    <math|\<partial\><rsub|q>\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>=<around|(|B<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|)><rsup|\<circ\>>>. Hence

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-D\><rsup|o><rsub|q>=\<Pi\><rprime|'><around*|(|\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M<rsup|<around|[|2|]>>,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>|]>-\<cal-T\><rsub|q><around|[|M<rsup|<around|[|3|]>>,\<ell\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>|]>|)>:
    </equation*>

    nonlinear part and a <strong|centred linear part>
    <math|\<cal-E\><rsup|c><rsub|q>y>; the scalar part vanishes by the mass equation.

    <\myframed>
      One loop with <math|\<delta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>> and
      <math|\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|3|]>>-\<Theta\><rsup|<around|[|2|]>>> inserted, <strong|without a scale
      integration>:

      <\equation*>
        <math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<cal-D\><rsup|o><rsub|q>|)>\<lesssim\>\<lambda\><rsup|5>q<rsup|-3>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-E\><rsup|c><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q><rsup|4>.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Why stop after two corrections?>

The constant and scalar linear jets of the defect vanish, so on the field ball

    <\equation*>
      <around|\||b<rsub|s>|\|>\<lesssim\>s<rsup|-1><around|(|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<cal-D\><rsub|s>|)>r<rsub|s><rsup|3>+<around|\<\|\|\>|\<cal-E\><rsup|c><rsub|s>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|<math-up|row>>r<rsub|s>|)>,<space|2em>Z<rsub|q>\<approx\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>><frac|s|q>b<rsub|s>\<mathd\>s.
    </equation*>

    Both terms have the same size; <math|s/q> is the backward transport. The cubic source:

    <center|<data-table|<tformat|<table|<row|<cell|corrections>|<cell|<math|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|\<cal-D\><rsub|s>|)>>>|<cell|backward source integral>>|<row|<cell|0: seed>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|3>s<rsup|-2>>>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|3/2>q<rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-1/2>\<mathd\>s=\<infty\>>>>|<row|<cell|1>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|4>s<rsup|-5/2>>>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|5/2>q<rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-1>\<mathd\>s=\<infty\>>>>|<row|<cell|2>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|5>s<rsup|-3>>>|<cell|<math|\<lambda\><rsup|7/2>q<rsup|-1><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>s<rsup|-3/2>\<mathd\>s=2\<lambda\><rsup|7/2>q<rsup|-3/2>>>>>>>>

    <\myframed>
      One correction is logarithmically borderline. <strong|Two corrections
      beyond the seed suffice> for the bounded-field source estimate.
    </myframed>

    <small|Each step costs two field derivatives: keep the iteration finite.
    Full estimates: Lecture<nbsp>7.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The corrections in graphs>

    <with|par-mode|center|<\script-output|tikz|default>
    \\documentclass[tikz]{standalone}

    \\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}

    \\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}

    \\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}

    \\usetikzlibrary{calc}

    \\tikzset{

     line/.style={thick},

     full/.style={double,double distance=1.3pt,thick},

     vtx/.style={circle,fill=black,inner sep=1.4pt},

     blob/.style={circle,draw,thick,fill=black!15,minimum size=4.2mm,inner sep=0pt},

     root/.style={line width=1.1pt,-latex},

     cross/.style={circle,draw,thick,fill=white,inner sep=0pt,minimum size=2.4mm,

       path picture={\\draw[thick] (path picture bounding box.north west)--(path picture bounding box.south east)

       (path picture bounding box.north east)--(path picture bounding box.south west);}},

     lab/.style={font=\\footnotesize,align=center},

    }

    % \\base{x}{y}: outer loop of bare lines G_q at (x,y), cross on top, root leg below

    \\newcommand\\loopc[2]{%

     \\draw[line] (#1,#2) circle (.45);

     \\node[cross] at (#1,#2+.45) {};}

    \\newcommand\\base[2]{\\loopc{#1}{#2}\\draw[root] (#1,#2-.45)--++(0,-.38);}

    % \\lineins{x}{y}{depth}: a correction inserted on the right line

    \\newcommand\\lineins[3]{%

     \\node[vtx] at (#1+.45,#2) {};

     \\draw[line] (#1+.67,#2) circle (.22);

     \\ifnum#3<gtr>1 \\node[vtx] at (#1+.89,#2) {}; \\draw[line] (#1+.99,#2) circle (.1);\\fi

     \\node[vtx] at (#1,#2-.45) {};}

    % \\vtxins{x}{y}{depth}: a correction as the vertex

    \\newcommand\\vtxins[3]{%

     \\draw[line] (#1,#2-.67) circle (.22);

     \\draw[root] (#1,#2-.89)--++(0,-.3);

     \\ifnum#3<gtr>1 \\node[vtx] at (#1+.22,#2-.67) {}; \\draw[line] (#1+.32,#2-.67) circle (.1);\\fi}

    \\begin{document}

    \\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\\small]

    % ---------------- (a) one step

    \\node[anchor=west] at (-1.2,1.3) {\\textbf{(a)} one step of the iteration};

    \\node at (.35,0) {$\\partial_q\\ell^{[j+1]}_q\\;=\\;-\\tfrac12\\,\\Pi$};

    \\draw[full] (2.35,.08) circle (.5);

    \\node[cross] at (2.35,.58) {};

    \\node[blob] (b) at (2.35,-.42) {};

    \\draw[root] (b.south)--++(0,-.35);

    \\begin{scope}[xshift=3.7cm,font=\\footnotesize]

     \\node[blob,minimum size=3mm] at (0,.55) {}; \\node[anchor=west] at (.25,.55) {vertex $D^2(U'+\\ell^{[j]})$};

     \\draw[full] (-.18,.05)--(.18,.05); \\node[anchor=west] at (.25,.05) {line $R=(K_q+M^{[j]}_q+D(U'+\\ell^{[j]}))^{-1}$};

     \\node[cross] at (0,-.45) {}; \\node[anchor=west] at (.25,-.45) {$\\partial_qK_q=1$, the derivative of the scale};

     \\draw[root] (-.18,-.95)--(.18,-.95); \\node[anchor=west] at (.25,-.95) {root: the output slot of the force};

    \\end{scope}

    \\node[lab,anchor=west] at (3.45,-1.45) {$\\ell^{[j]}$, $j\\geq 1$, enters twice: in the lines and in the vertex};

    % ---------------- (b) expansion in bare lines

    \\begin{scope}[yshift=-3.4cm]

    \\node[anchor=west] at (-1.2,1.25) {\\textbf{(b)} expanded in bare lines $G_q=(K_q+DU')^{-1}$ \\ (single lines; external field legs not drawn)};

    % seed

    \\base{0}{0}\\node[vtx] at (0,-.45) {};

    \\node[lab] at (0,-1.6) {seed $\\delta^{[1]}=\\ell^{[1]}$\\\\one loop, $\\lambda g_q$};

    % delta 1

    \\node at (1.15,0) {$\\longrightarrow$};

    \\base{2.15}{0}\\lineins{2.15}{0}{1}

    \\node at (3.35,0) {$+$};

    \\loopc{4.2}{0}\\vtxins{4.2}{0}{1}

    \\node[lab] at (3.2,-1.6) {$\\delta^{[2]}$: $\\ell^{[1]}$ inserted\\\\two loops, $\\lambda g_q^2$};

    % delta 2

    \\node at (5.25,0) {$\\longrightarrow$};

    \\base{6.25}{0}\\lineins{6.25}{0}{2}

    \\node at (7.6,0) {$+$};

    \\loopc{8.45}{0}\\vtxins{8.45}{0}{2}

    \\node[lab] at (7.4,-1.6) {$\\delta^{[3]}$: $\\delta^{[2]}$ inserted\\\\three loops, $\\lambda g_q^3$};

    % stop

    \\node at (9.75,0) {$\\Longrightarrow$};

    \\base{10.95}{0}\\node[vtx] at (10.95,-.45) {};

    \\node[vtx] at (11.4,0) {}; \\node[blob,fill=black!30,minimum size=5.2mm] at (11.66,0) {};

    \\node[font=\\scriptsize] at (11.66,0) {$\\delta^{\\![3]}$};

    \\node[lab] at (11.15,-1.6) {defect $\\mathcal D^{\\rm o}_q$, no $q$-integral\\\\$\\mathsf S_4(\\mathcal D^{\\rm o}_q)\\lesssim\\lambda^5q^{-3}$};

    \\end{scope}

    \\end{tikzpicture}

